TRANSFORMER (encoder-decoder) — types & fundamentals
====================================================
Token ids: int64
Embeddings: float32 [seq_len, d_model]   d_model=512 typical
Positional encoding: float32, added (not concatenated)
Attention scores: float32 [heads, seq, seq]  softmax over last dim
FFN hidden: float32 [seq, d_ff]            d_ff=2048 typical
LayerNorm: float32, residual Add & Norm
N = 6 stacked layers (paper default)

Inputs
  |
  v
Input Embedding  +  Positional Encoding
  |
  +-------------------------------+
  |  Multi-Head Attention         |
  |  Add & Norm                   |  Nx
  |  Feed Forward                 |
  |  Add & Norm                   |
  +-------------------------------+
  |                               |
  |                               v
  |                    Masked Multi-Head Attention
  |                    Add & Norm
  |                    Multi-Head Attention (encoder K,V)
  |                    Add & Norm
  |                    Feed Forward
  |                    Add & Norm          Nx
  |                               |
Outputs (shifted right)           |
  |                               |
  v                               v
Output Embedding + Positional Encoding
  |
  v
Linear  ->  Softmax  ->  Output Probabilities


RANKING SERVICE + CASSANDRA — types & fundamentals
==================================================
user_id:            string / uuid
ranking_query:      structured request (features + context)
ranked_results:     list[(item_id, score)]  score=float32
query_latency_sla:  < 20 ms average
consistency:        99.999%  (Cassandra QUORUM / LOCAL_QUORUM typical)
throughput:         billions of queries
storage:            Cassandra wide-column, partitioned by user or item

